$ mp contacts --help
Contact index operations

Usage: mp contacts [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  search   Search the contact index
  rebuild  Rebuild the contact index from the local message store now (every configured account unless `-A` names one)
  stats    Show index statistics
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>  Account to use
  -h, --help               Print help

The index is a cache per account, `contacts-cache.json` in the account's data
directory, ranked from the From, To, Cc and Bcc headers of the stored mail.
Every sync and every send folds the mail it saw into it. The first search or
stats of an account builds it before answering, and rebuilds it first when
another mp version's extractor built it, so a reinstall never keeps an index
the current rules would not produce; the CLI, the TUI and the desktop app
read it the same way. `mp contacts rebuild` rebuilds it on demand.

$ mp contacts search --help
Search the contact index

Usage: mp contacts search [OPTIONS] [QUERY]

Arguments:
  [QUERY]  Query string (fuzzy-matched against name and email)

Options:
      --parsable           Emit tab-delimited `email\tname` lines (for mutt/aerc/vim integration)
      --json               Emit one JSON object {account, query, contacts: [{address, display_name, sent_to, sent_cc, received}]}, best match first
  -n, --limit <LIMIT>      Max number of results [default: 20]
  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>  Account to use
  -h, --help               Print help

