$ mp signature --help
Manage the signatures drafts carry, and each account's default

Usage: mp signature [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list     List the signatures, marking the account's default
  show     Print a signature's content
  new      Create an empty signature and print the path of its file
  edit     Open a signature in $EDITOR
  rename   Rename a signature
  delete   Delete a signature
  default  Print the account's default signature, or set it, or clear it with --none
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>  Account to use
  -h, --help               Print help

A signature is one Markdown file the daemon keeps under the configuration
directory; `mp new -s <name>` and the TUI's and the desktop app's compose
dialogs splice it into a draft. The default is per account: `-A` names the
account, the first configured one otherwise.

Examples:
  mp signature list
  mp signature new work && mp signature edit work
  mp -A tum signature default work

