$ mp calendar --help
Calendar / iMIP invite operations

Usage: mp calendar [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  rebuild  Report what the stored attendee REPLY emails resolve on the stored invitations. Writes nothing: attendee statuses are derived from the `invite.ics` payloads wherever they are displayed, so there is no cached copy to rebuild. Covers every configured account unless `-A` names one
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>  Account to use
  -h, --help               Print help

$ mp calendar rebuild --help
Report what the stored attendee REPLY emails resolve on the stored invitations. Writes nothing: attendee statuses are derived from the `invite.ics` payloads wherever they are displayed, so there is no cached copy to rebuild. Covers every configured account unless `-A` names one

Usage: mp calendar rebuild [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>  Account to use
  -h, --help               Print help

$ mp hooks --help
Inspect, dry-run and replay the mail hooks of `[[accounts.hooks]]`

Usage: mp hooks [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list    List the hooks with their cursor and last run (every configured account unless `-A` names one)
  test    Check a hook against a stored message; runs nothing, moves no cursor
  replay  Run a hook for a stored message now, whatever its cursor says (the `match` table still has to pass)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>  Account to use
  -h, --help               Print help

The daemon runs a hook's command once for every message that arrives after
the hook was first seen and passes its `match` table. See
docs/daemon-operations.md for the configuration and the JSON on stdin.

Examples:
  mp hooks list
  mp hooks test pi-remote 'mp://assistant/inbox/abc@example.com'
  mp hooks replay pi-remote 'mp://assistant/inbox/abc@example.com'

$ mp hooks list --help
List the hooks with their cursor and last run (every configured account unless `-A` names one)

Usage: mp hooks list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json               Print the daemon's answer as JSON
  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>  Account to use
  -h, --help               Print help

