$ mp store --help
Local store maintenance (retention garbage collection)

Usage: mp store [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  gc    Run the retention sweep now: evict cached blobs over the disk cap
  help  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>  Account to use
  -h, --help               Print help

$ mp store gc --help
Run the retention sweep now: evict cached blobs over the disk cap.

The first over-cap run only warns and records a marker; run it again to evict. `--dry-run` prints what would go without touching anything. A run that would reclaim more than half the store's blob bytes is refused without `--force` (a fat-finger guard while on-demand re-fetch, #0085, does not yet exist).

Usage: mp store gc [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --dry-run
          Print what would be evicted and stop; change nothing

      --force
          Evict even when the plan would reclaim more than half the store

      --all-accounts
          Sweep every configured account rather than just the default / `-A`

  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>
          Account to use

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

$ mp cutover --help
Report what is left of the file-era `.md` tree, and import its drafts.

Assigns an `id:` frontmatter field to any draft that has none, so a file-era draft becomes addressable by selector, then names the file-era mailbox directories nothing reads any more and prints the command that removes them. It deletes nothing itself. `--dry-run` writes not even the `id:` field. Covers every configured account unless `-A` names one.

Usage: mp cutover [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --dry-run
          Report only; write nothing at all

  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>
          Account to use

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

$ mp dump-keys --help
Dump the TUI key bindings from the single KEYMAP source of truth.

Markdown by default; `--json` emits the section-grouped shape the website consumes. Regenerate the site data with: `mp dump-keys --json > website/src/data/tui-keys.json` (see scripts/regen-website-keys.sh).

Usage: mp dump-keys [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json
          Emit JSON grouped by section instead of Markdown

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

$ mp dump-mailbox --help
Dump message envelopes from the local message store as NDJSON.

Offline: reads the local store only, never the network. One compact JSON object per line, with the fields account, mailbox, message_id, from, to, cc, subject, date_sort, flags, attachments (name + size) and invite. No filesystem paths appear in the output.

Records are sorted by account, mailbox, date_sort, message_id and subject (the message's uid breaks remaining ties without being emitted), so two runs over an unchanged store are byte-identical.

Dumps every configured account by default; `-A/--account` restricts it to one, `--mailbox` to the named mailboxes.

Usage: mp dump-mailbox [OPTIONS] --json

Options:
      --json
          Emit newline-delimited JSON. Currently the only output format, and required, so a later default cannot silently change this one

      --mailbox <MAILBOX>
          Mailbox to dump (role, slug or sidebar label; repeatable). Default: every mailbox of every selected account

  -A, --account <ACCOUNT>
          Account to use

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

